For a companion test, let the load succeed, let the device refuse the first store attempt, then accept the second. There must be just one log entry. A split request/response interface would need a different policy: acceptance and completion are then distinct, and an outstanding request cannot be sent again while waiting for acknowledgment. In particular, ignoring responses from squashed ordinary reads does not undo the effects of a device read. Model this distinction before comparing simulators or changing a memory schedule.
